1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,643
In this town, you only get one hundred words per day.

2
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:07,731
Everyone has a counter on their chest.

3
00:00:08,827 --> 00:00:11,198
Every word you say, it goes down.

4
00:00:12,293 --> 00:00:15,574
When it hits zero, your voice is gone until tomorrow.

5
00:00:17,127 --> 00:00:18,892
So nobody wastes words here.

6
00:00:19,693 --> 00:00:20,852
No small talk.

7
00:00:21,693 --> 00:00:23,155
No "how are you."

8
00:00:23,827 --> 00:00:24,683
Just nods.

9
00:00:25,827 --> 00:00:28,804
My little sister Pia spends her words on singing.

10
00:00:30,227 --> 00:00:32,598
Every morning. All one hundred of them.

11
00:00:33,693 --> 00:00:36,671
Then she's quiet for the rest of the day.

12
00:00:38,093 --> 00:00:39,858
Dad says she's wasting them.

13
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:43,637
Pia says songs are the only words worth saying.

14
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:47,431
Then the mayor announced a new rule.

15
00:00:48,527 --> 00:00:49,989
Words don't reset anymore.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:53,637
Whatever you have left... is all you'll ever get.

17
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:56,825
The whole town went silent.

18
00:00:57,627 --> 00:00:59,089
People started hoarding words.

19
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:00,616
Selling them.

20
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:02,616
Stealing them.

21
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:05,222
I had forty-two left.

22
00:01:05,893 --> 00:01:07,052
Pia had zero.

23
00:01:07,893 --> 00:01:09,962
She had already sung that morning.

24
00:01:10,927 --> 00:01:12,692
She would never speak again.

25
00:01:13,493 --> 00:01:15,865
She just looked at me and smiled.

26
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,331
That night, I found the mayor's office.

27
00:01:20,427 --> 00:01:21,586
A giant machine.

28
00:01:22,427 --> 00:01:23,586
Full of words.

29
00:01:24,427 --> 00:01:25,586
Millions of them.

30
00:01:26,427 --> 00:01:27,283
Everyone's words.

31
00:01:28,427 --> 00:01:29,889
He wasn't saving them.

32
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:32,022
He was collecting them.

33
00:01:32,693 --> 00:01:34,155
For one giant speech.

34
00:01:34,827 --> 00:01:38,107
One that would make everyone in town obey him forever.

35
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:41,122
I had forty-two words.

36
00:01:41,793 --> 00:01:43,255
I needed exactly one.

37
00:01:43,927 --> 00:01:45,389
I pressed the microphone.

38
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:47,219
And I sang.

39
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,219
The machine cracked.

40
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:51,825
Words flew out like birds.

41
00:01:52,627 --> 00:01:53,786
Back to everyone.

42
00:01:54,627 --> 00:01:56,089
Pia opened her mouth.

43
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:59,131
And she sang the whole morning song.

44
00:02:00,227 --> 00:02:01,992
My counter says zero now.

45
00:02:02,793 --> 00:02:03,952
I don't mind.

46
00:02:04,793 --> 00:02:07,165
She talks enough for both of us.

